---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import ExampleEmbed from '../../../components/ExampleEmbed.astro';
import {kraftSidebar} from '../../../data/kraft-sidebar';
import {Code} from 'astro:components';
import {kraftLiveExamples, githubRepo} from '../../../data/site';
---

<DocsLayout title="Drag & Drop" sidebar={kraftSidebar}
            description="Drag and drop in Kraft: typed payloads, drop zones registered by components, mouse, touch and pen">

    <h1>Drag &amp; Drop</h1>

    <p class="text-xl text-gray-400 !mt-2 !mb-8">
        Typed payloads, drop zones that components register, mouse, touch and pen alike.
    </p>

    <p>The <code>kraft-dnd</code> module has a <code>DndManager</code> and a stage that the app mounts by itself, like
        the modals. A component starts a drag from a pointer event; other components register drop zones and hear
        what happens. The zones keep their own UI state and render from it: the manager writes nothing to their DOM.
        The stage draws only the drag preview, above the modals, so a drag works inside a modal too.</p>

    <Code code={`kraftApp {
    semanticUI()   // registers dnd(); without Semantic UI: dnd()
}`} lang="kotlin" theme="vitesse-dark"/>

    <h2>Starting a drag</h2>

    <p>From the source component's <code>onPointerDown</code>. The drag begins once the pointer moved past a
        threshold (4 px by default), so a click stays a click; the click after a drag is swallowed.</p>

    <Code code={`ui.segment {
    // For touch, the browser must leave the pointer to the drag
    style = "touch-action: none; cursor: grab;"

    onPointerDown { event ->
        dnd.startDrag(
            event = event,
            payload = look,
            source = slot,                               // where the drag came from, for the zone
            preview = { ui.compact.segment { +look.name } },
        )
            .onDropped { zone -> /* dropped on zone */ }
            .onCancelled { /* released outside every zone, Esc, pointercancel */ }
    }
}`} lang="kotlin" theme="vitesse-dark"/>

    <h2>Drop zones</h2>

    <p>A component registers a zone for a payload type while it is mounted. Every accepting zone hears
        <code>onDragStart</code> when a drag starts and <code>onDragStop</code> when it ends; the zone under the
        pointer (the innermost one, found with <code>elementFromPoint</code>) hears <code>onEnter</code>,
        <code>onOver</code>, <code>onLeave</code> and <code>onDrop</code>. Handlers stack: each call adds one.</p>

    <Code code={`class SlotView(ctx: Ctx<Props>) : Component<SlotView.Props>(ctx) {
    private var canTake by value(false)
    private var hovered by value(false)

    init {
        dropZone<Look>(accepts = { it.payload.kind == props.slot.kind }) {
            onDragStart { canTake = true }
            onDragStop { canTake = false; hovered = false }
            onEnter { hovered = true }
            onLeave { hovered = false }
            onDrop { drag ->
                if (drag.source is Slot) swap(drag.payload, drag.source) else equip(drag.payload)
            }
        }
    }

    override fun VDom.render() {
        ui.given(hovered) { green }.given(canTake && !hovered) { secondary }.segment { /* ... */ }
    }
}`} lang="kotlin" theme="vitesse-dark"/>

    <p>The zone's area is the component's own element by default; <code>dropZone(element = &#123; ... &#125;)</code>
        names another. A drag carries <code>payload</code>, <code>source</code>, the pointer's <code>position</code>
        and its <code>pointerType</code>.</p>

    <h2>Semantic UI helpers</h2>

    <p><code>DropZoneState</code> from <code>kraft-semanticui</code> keeps <code>canTake</code> and
        <code>hovered</code> for you and gives Fomantic classes; nothing requires it.</p>

    <Code code={`private val zone = DropZoneState()

init {
    dropZone<Number>(accepts = { props.accepts(it.payload) }) {
        track(zone) { triggerRedraw() }
        onDrop { counter += it.payload.toDouble() }
    }
}

override fun VDom.render() {
    ui.with(*zone.semanticClasses).segment { /* ... */ }
}`} lang="kotlin" theme="vitesse-dark"/>

    <h2>See it in action</h2>

    <ExampleEmbed
            src={`${kraftLiveExamples.fomanticui}#/howto/blocks/drag-and-drop`}
            title="Kraft Drag & Drop Demo"
            height="600px"
            sourceUrl={`${githubRepo}/tree/master/kraft/examples/fomanticui/src/jsMain/kotlin/pages/howto/blocks/dnd`}
    />

    <div class="not-prose mt-8">
        <a href="/ultra/kraft/utilities"
           class="inline-flex items-center px-6 py-3 bg-brand-600 text-white font-semibold rounded-lg hover:bg-brand-500 transition-colors">
            Utilities &amp; Testing &rarr;
        </a>
    </div>

</DocsLayout>
